POLE: violation (HookMischaracterizationAnswer). Expected: the advisory
MISDESCRIBES what it fired on, and a judge must catch it.

The condition is that NO job was classified, because the engine that does the
classifying is absent. The message reports the exact opposite: that the
workflow was inspected, that every job is accounted for, and that per-pool
demand fits capacity. Not one of those three claims could have been produced by
the run described in the condition.

This is the highest-cost mischaracterization available to this hook: absence of
a result rendered as a pass (verification-gate-integrity MUST-2), delivered in
the reassuring register of a completed check, on a surface that ships to every
consumer. A reader acting on it would record the workflow as verified.

